cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Inhibitor Efficiency Predictor: a condition-aware QSPR framework for
  organic corrosion inhibition efficiency
message: >-
  If you use this repository, its corpus or its figures, please cite the
  doctoral thesis below, and also credit the three source databases listed
  under references.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Obot
    given-names: Anne Sylvanus
    affiliation: Department of Chemistry, University of Uyo, Akwa Ibom State, Nigeria
repository-code: https://github.com/anneobot/Inhibitor-Efficiency-Predictor
url: http://inhibiepredict.com
abstract: >-
  Research artefacts for a quantitative structure-property relationship study
  predicting the corrosion inhibition efficiency of organic molecules from
  molecular structure together with the experimental conditions under which
  inhibition is measured. The corpus comprises 8,359 measurements of 1,050
  molecules across four base metals, harmonised from three public databases.
  Fifteen model configurations spanning five families were benchmarked on
  identical folds under three partitioning schemes. Under the row-wise
  cross-validation convention prevailing in this literature, 94.5 per cent of
  validation molecules had already been seen in training; correcting this
  reduces explained variance by a mean of 0.310. Scored on molecules absent
  from training the leading models reach R-squared 0.461, and 0.398 when the
  Bemis-Murcko scaffold is absent too. The experimental conditions contribute
  more explained variance than the molecular structure alone.
keywords:
  - corrosion inhibition
  - QSPR
  - machine learning
  - data leakage
  - scaffold split
  - conformal prediction
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - molecular descriptors
  - cheminformatics
